# What this repository tracks, and what it does not.
#
# TRACKED, on purpose, and excluded by nothing below:
#   data/      every input instance (gzipped) and data/MANIFEST.tsv
#   results/   every per-run record of the published study, PROVENANCE.md and logs/ (the self-test,
#              statistics, data and verification logs, and the progress log of the original runs)
# They are the input and the evidence behind every table, figure and quoted number in the article.
#
# Everything listed here is regenerated by building, by a rerun or by the analysis.

# ---- build output -------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
build*/
runs/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
compile_commands.json
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# ---- Python bytecode ----------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---- generated by the analysis ------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloned on its own, analyse.py finds no main.tex above it and writes these inside the
# repository rather than beside the paper.  They are derived from results/ and are rebuilt by
#   python3 scripts/analyse.py
tables/
figures/

# A reader's own runs: scripts/run_all.sh writes a full rerun to results-rerun/ and a --quick smoke
# test to results-quick/, so that neither can overwrite the published records in results/.
results-quick/
results-rerun/

# ---- expanded instance files ------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ ships gzipped (with data/MANIFEST.tsv); plain-text copies written by
# `experiments instances --data data` are regenerable and not tracked.
data/*.txt

# ---- editor and OS noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
